                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " “What do you think? A man had two sons; and he went to the first and said, ‘Son, go and work in the vineyard today.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.21.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.21.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 21:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he answered, ‘I will not’; but afterward he repented and went. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.21.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.21.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 21:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he went to the second and said the same; and he answered, ‘I go, sir,’ but did not go. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.21.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.21.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 21:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Which of the two did the will of his father?” They said, “The first.” Jesus said to them, “Truly, I say to you, the tax collectors and the harlots go into the kingdom of God before you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.21.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.21.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 21:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LUK.7.29+LUK.7.30"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Lk 7.29-30",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " For John came to you in the way of righteousness, and you did not believe him, but the tax collectors and the harlots believed him; and even when you saw it, you did not afterward repent and believe him.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.21.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.21.32"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
